{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"bf092c76357c8275","name":"card_event_hidden_plans","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/CovertOp/events/card_event_hidden_plans","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"HIDDEN PLANS","text":"Choose One - Draw a Covert unit OR reveal a Covert unit and give it +1+1.","flavorText":"One notable example of USA’s hidden plans during WWII is the Manhattan Project, a top-secret initiative to develop nuclear weapons. Led by scientists such as J. Robert Oppenheimer, the project resulted in the successful creation of atomic bombs, which were ultimately used against Japan in 1945. The goal was to keep the entire atomic bomb program secret from Germany and Japan which Manhattan Project security officials accomplished successfully. They also tried to keep word of the atomic bomb from reaching the Soviet Union despite them being their allies. Secrecy in the Manhattan Project was so complete that many people working for the organization did not know what they were working on until they heard about the bombing of Hiroshima on the radio.","faction":"USA","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_hidden_plans","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_hidden_plans_title","SourceString":"HIDDEN PLANS","LocalizedString":"HIDDEN PLANS"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_hidden_plans_text","SourceString":"Choose One - Draw a Covert unit OR reveal a Covert unit and give it +1+1.","LocalizedString":"Choose One - Draw a Covert unit OR reveal a Covert unit and give it +1+1."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_hidden_plans_history","SourceString":"One notable example of USA’s hidden plans during WWII is the Manhattan Project, a top-secret initiative to develop nuclear weapons. Led by scientists such as J. Robert Oppenheimer, the project resulted in the successful creation of atomic bombs, which were ultimately used against Japan in 1945. The goal was to keep the entire atomic bomb program secret from Germany and Japan which Manhattan Project security officials accomplished successfully. They also tried to keep word of the atomic bomb from reaching the Soviet Union despite them being their allies. Secrecy in the Manhattan Project was so complete that many people working for the organization did not know what they were working on until they heard about the bombing of Hiroshima on the radio.","LocalizedString":"One notable example of USA’s hidden plans during WWII is the Manhattan Project, a top-secret initiative to develop nuclear weapons. Led by scientists such as J. Robert Oppenheimer, the project resulted in the successful creation of atomic bombs, which were ultimately used against Japan in 1945. The goal was to keep the entire atomic bomb program secret from Germany and Japan which Manhattan Project security officials accomplished successfully. They also tried to keep word of the atomic bomb from reaching the Soviet Union despite them being their allies. Secrecy in the Manhattan Project was so complete that many people working for the organization did not know what they were working on until they heard about the bombing of Hiroshima on the radio."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::CurrentExpansion","isReserved":true,"chooseOneCards":[{"cardText":{"Namespace":"","Key":"D0552EA9438313ED45465D9D3D396559","SourceString":"Draw a Covert unit from your deck.","LocalizedString":"Draw a Covert unit from your deck."},"selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":false},{"cardText":{"Namespace":"","Key":"AD925AA0454A24EFC414DCAF8DF335E5","SourceString":"Reveal a Covert unit and give it +1+1.","LocalizedString":"Reveal a Covert unit and give it +1+1."},"selectTargetOnPlayedFromHand":true}],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content